summaries to differ semantically: detailed preserves tool-activity receipts and brief preserves outcomes only. The implemented summary handler in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:126-145 reads only member projections and passes the same { memberProjections } shape to both provider operations. The provider double in packages/lhc/test/fixtures/provider-double.ts:148-153 derives both summaries from the same joined projection text with only the operation marker differing. The TC-3.8 test in packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts:481-507 uses a simple prompt/answer turn, asserts only distinct detailed()/brief() marked content, and never creates a tool-run receipt fixture or asserts that detailed carries receipt content while brief strips to outcomes. This leaves a required TC-3.8 assertion unverified.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/provider-double.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.8\",\"TC-3.8\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-3.8-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"TC-3.8 does not prove detailed summaries preserve receipts while brief summaries preserve outcomes only\",\"evidence\":\"Story lines 44-45 require detailed and brief chunk summaries to differ semantically: detailed preserves tool-activity receipts and brief preserves outcomes only. The implemented summary handler in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:126-145 reads only member projections and passes the same { memberProjections } shape to both provider operations. The provider double in packages/lhc/test/fixtures/provider-double.ts:148-153 derives both summaries from the same joined projection text with only the operation marker differing. The TC-3.8 test in packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts:481-507 uses a simple prompt/answer turn, asserts only distinct detailed()/brief() marked content, and never creates a tool-run receipt fixture or asserts that detailed carries receipt content while brief strips to outcomes. This leaves a required TC-3.8 assertion unverified.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/provider-double.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.8\",\"TC-3.8\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-3.1 / TC-3.1: closed turn drains to ready turn_rendering and lower_band_projection independent rows.\",\"AC-3.2 / TC-3.2: failed smoothing falls back to raw prompt, rendering remains ready, and gap records message/form.\",\"AC-3.3 / TC-3.3: repaired smoothing does not mutate the existing gapped rendering; explicit direct requeue rebuilds and clears the gap.\",\"AC-3.4 / TC-3.4: captured composeTurnRendering input carries ordered tool parts with outcomes including the failed call.\",\"AC-3.5 / TC-3.5: turn read-back includes stored chunkId and memberIdx after derivation.\",\"AC-3.6 / TC-3.6: accumulated crossing closes the prior chunk and starts the incoming turn in the next chunk, including threshold equality coverage.\",\"AC-3.7 / TC-3.7: oversized projection self-chunks and closes immediately, including the behind-open-chunk case.\",\"AC-3.8 partial: close queues detailed and brief summary work as separate items with independent states/retry/requeue behavior.\",\"AC-3.9 / TC-3.9: replayed identical event streams produce identical chunk/chunk_member snapshots and summary artifacts.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-3.8 / TC-3.8: detailed summary preserving tool-activity receipts while brief summary preserves outcomes only is not evidenced by code or tests.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm vitest run test/derivation-turns.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"com